<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter Tali Coleman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1919–1997</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter Tali Coleman was an American Samoan politician who became the first person of Samoan descent to be appointed governor, in 1956, and the territory's first elected governor in 1977. He served further elected terms until 1993 and also held senior posts in the Trust Territory of the Pacific Islands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-tali-coleman.jpg" alt="Peter Tali Coleman" width="307" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TTPI(Trust Territory of the Pacific Islands) Headquarters · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Tali_Coleman.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
